  "body": "The Bore operation always enters a hole with a straight plunge\r\n(`crates/app/src/operation/generate.rs`, the Bore arm: `entry: Entry3D::Plunge`).\r\nThe motion kernel already supports Ramp and Helix for bores\r\n(`crates/motion/tests/bore_ramp_angle.rs`). The user cannot select them.\r\n\r\nA second problem stops a ramp on a small hole. The kernel ring ramp allows at most\r\n64 out-and-back legs (`MAX_ZIG_LEGS`). A 3.2 mm hole with a 3.175 mm tool has a\r\ncutter-centre ring of 0.0125 mm radius. A 5 degree ramp needs about 73 legs for 1 mm of\r\nstepdown. The ramp gives up and the tool dives axially. Measured on main: Ramp and Helix\r\non that hole post 6 axial dives and the note \"the ring is too short to ramp at the angle\".\r\n\r\nNeeded:\r\n- `entry` on the Bore operation: plunge (default), ramp, helix.\r\n- The links' approach `ramp_angle` and `helix_angle` cap every descent of the hole.\r\n- The default stays plunge. A plunge Bore is written without an `entry` word, so\r\n  earlier files do not change.\r\n- A hole barely wider than the tool (ring radius 0.0125 mm) ramps at the cap.\r\n- Arc is refused by name.\r\n\r\nDone means:\r\n- One Bore operation with entry ramp and angle 5 posts no feed descent steeper than\r\n  5 degrees on holes from 3.2 mm to 6 mm with a 3.175 mm tool.\r\n- The only axial move is the re-plunge down the column that the ring just cut, one for\r\n  each level, and a note names it.\r\n- A non-centre-cutting tool with the default (plunge) entry is still refused by name.\r\n\r\nProposed labels (a collaborator sets them): enhancement, source:agent, P6, effort:high, area:2d\r\n",
